This crate (`symphonia-codec-evrc`) is a pure-Rust EVRC (Enhanced Variable Rate Codec, Service
Option 3) decoder. It is licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of
Project Symphonia.

The decoder is a port of FFmpeg's EVRC decoder (`libavcodec/evrcdec.c`, `libavcodec/evrcdata.h`),
which implements TIA/EIA/IS-127 ("Enhanced Variable Rate Codec, Speech Service Option 3 for Wideband
Spread Spectrum Digital Systems"). The LSP vector quantizer codebooks and the rate 1/8 energy
quantizer (`src/tables.rs`) are extracted programmatically from FFmpeg's `evrcdata.h`. The weighted
vector sum and the LSF to LSP conversion follow `libavcodec/acelp_vectors.c` and
`libavcodec/lsp.c`. These files are distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or later.

